Fictional Band Name: The Bend Census

Band Description: The Bend Census is a four-member ensemble built around the idea that pitch movement can be measured without becoming mechanical.

Mai An — đàn bầu, natural harmonics, long controlled bends, volume swells, pitch-rod articulation.
Leon Bui — LinnDrum programming, mono-synth bass, muted electric bass, live arrangement cuts.
Celeste Ho — Rhodes, clavinet, vibraphone, harmonic voicing and chord-duration control.
Elias Tran — muted trumpet, bass clarinet, occasional pizzicato cello, overtone cueing.

There is no conventional lead singer and almost no fixed solo hierarchy. Mai establishes the harmonic field, but the others determine how clearly or ambiguously the listener perceives it. Leon can clarify a pitch with bass, Celeste can destabilize it with a suspended electric-piano voicing, and Elias can expose an upper partial by entering on one carefully chosen note. Live sets are arranged through eye contact and hand signals rather than backing tracks.

